{% doc %}
  Inline SVG icon, drawn on a 24×24 grid.

  UI icons are original line drawings (1.75 stroke, round caps/joins) that inherit
  `currentColor`, so they follow the text colour of whatever contains them, including
  the high-contrast mode of the accessibility panel. Brand marks (whatsapp, facebook,
  instagram, telegram, tiktok, youtube) are used only as links to those services;
  their paths come from the CC0-licensed simple-icons project (https://simpleicons.org).

  Icons are decorative by default (`aria-hidden="true"`, `focusable="false"`): the
  control that contains the icon must carry the accessible name. Pass `label` only
  for a stand-alone meaningful icon; it then gets `role="img"` and `aria-label`.
  An unknown `name` renders nothing.

  Names: cart, bag, search, account, heart, heart-filled, chevron-left, chevron-right,
  chevron-up, chevron-down, arrow-left, arrow-right, arrow-up, close, menu, plus, minus,
  zoom, location, phone, mail, clock, accessibility, check, info, alert, truck-off,
  store, shield, lock, credit-card, tag, bolt, star, trash, filter, sort, share,
  external, home, play, pause, spinner, whatsapp, facebook, instagram, telegram,
  tiktok, youtube.

  @param {string} name - Icon name (see list above).
  @param {number} [size] - Rendered width and height in px. Default 24.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes on the <svg>.
  @param {string} [label] - Accessible name for a meaningful stand-alone icon.

  @example
  {% render 'icon', name: 'cart' %}
  {% render 'icon', name: 'chevron-left', size: 16, class: 'carousel__icon' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign icon_size = size | default: 24
  assign icon_filled = false
  case name
    when 'heart-filled', 'star', 'whatsapp', 'facebook', 'instagram', 'telegram', 'tiktok', 'youtube'
      assign icon_filled = true
  endcase
-%}
{%- capture icon_body -%}
